  "body": "## What changed\n\n`project::save` now writes the project to a temporary file in the same\nfolder, flushes it, and renames it over the old file. It uses\n`machine::store::write_atomic`, which machine files, preferences, recent\nfiles and view settings already use. A failed save now keeps the old\nproject.\n\n- Two refusals of the old plain write stay: a folder that does not exist,\n  and a read-only project file. On Linux and macOS a rename replaces a\n  read-only file, so `project::save` checks first.\n- `machine::store::temp_path_for` gives the temp path. A path that names\n  no file is now refused by name before a folder is made.\n- The temp name has the process ID and a number for the calling thread.\n  Before, two saves of one file at the same moment (an autosave and a\n  save by the user) wrote the same temp file. Each thread takes its\n  number one time, from one counter. The saves of one thread run one\n  after another, so its name can repeat.\n- No change to the file format, `PROJECT_VERSION` or the saved text.\n- Decisions: `docs/decisions/3509-atomic-project-save.md`.\n\nThis branch starts at upstream/main `dc86a8c48`.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew in `crates/app/tests/project_roundtrip.rs`:\n\n- `a_project_save_replaces_the_file_and_leaves_no_temp_file`\n- `a_failed_project_save_keeps_the_old_file`\n- `a_project_save_into_a_missing_folder_is_refused_and_makes_no_folder`\n- `a_read_only_project_file_is_refused_and_kept`\n\nNew in `crates/app/tests/machine_edit.rs`:\n\n- `two_threads_never_share_a_temp_file`\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick` (Windows 11) on `dbe37ad2c`: green, 8 of 8 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled. The four new tests pass with the other 76 tests of `project_roundtrip`, and `two_threads_never_share_a_temp_file` passes with the other 12 tests of `machine_edit`. It ran the app unit\ntests and the suites `contour_dxf_sketch`, `import_step_open_shell`,\n`machine_edit`, `model_solid_ranges`, `project_roundtrip` and\n`sketch_project`.\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\nHeavy lanes: `cargo xtask gate heavy --dry-run` reaches every `app` heavy target (207 steps), because `crates/app/src` changed. I did not run them yet. I will run them on the final head before I mark this PR ready.\n\n## Known limits\n\n- A save over a project path that is a symbolic link replaces the link\n  with a regular file. The target of the link does not change.\n- The saved file gets the default permissions of a new file in that\n  folder, not the permissions, owner or ACL of the old file. Machine\n  files and preferences act the same way.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A real crash, full disk or lost network share during a write. The test\n  with a folder in the place of the temp file makes the same failure path.\n- A bare file name (`job.camproj`, no folder). Code inspection only: a\n  test would change the current folder of the test process.\n- Linux and macOS. The read-only check was run on Windows only.\n- Two threads that save one file at the same moment. On Windows, two\n  renames over one file at the same moment can fail for a reason that\n  is not the temp name, so the test checks the temp names instead.\n\nChangelog: Saving a project no longer destroys the old file when the write fails.\nEffort: low\n\nFixes #3509\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
